Subject: [PATCH] Honor footprint 3D model (scale (xyz ...)) via App::Link
 ScaleVector

KiCad allows a per-footprint scale on a 3D model. StepUp used to warn
"wrong scale!!! set scale to (1 1 1)" and import the model unscaled.

With Links enabled, a scaled instance is now placed as an App::Link whose
ScaleVector carries the KiCad scale. The scale is applied in model
coordinates before the model rotation/offset and the footprint placement,
matching KiCad's own 3D viewer / STEP export order.

- first (scaled) instance of a model: the imported unscaled model is
  relabeled SRC_<model>_<tstamp>, hidden, parked in a
  Scaled_Model_Sources<sfx> container under Step_Models, and the instance
  becomes a Link to it
- cached instances: existing Link path, ScaleVector set when non-unit
- unscaled instances of the same model keep ScaleVector (1 1 1)
- multi-part models (App::Part) work since Link scales the whole target
- warnings become info messages when the scale will be applied; the old
  warning and the "reset values of scale" popup stay when Links are off
- apply_model_scale = False restores the old behaviour
---
 kicadStepUptools.py | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 83 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

